.TH ABORT 3
.SH NAME
abort \- generate a fault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
abort()
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B abort
sends the program the signal SIGIOT, after setting its action back to
the default, so that the program ends and leaves an image of itself in
the file
.B core
in the current directory, for the debugger
.BR adb (1).
The streams of
.BR stdio (3)
are not flushed.
.PP
A program calls abort when it finds that something that cannot happen
has happened.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
abort does not return.
.SH SEE ALSO
adb(1), exit(2), signal(2)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B abort
function first appeared in Version 5 AT&T UNIX.
